KW  - LIMITED FEEDBACK
KW  - WIRELESS
KW  - DOWNLINK
KW  - DESIGN
KW  - PILOT
KW  - MODEL
AB  - Achieving high performance in Frequency Division Duplexing (FDD) massive Multiple-Input Multiple-Output (MIMO) systems is fundamentally challenged by channel state information (CSI) feedback overhead and channel aging, particularly in mobile environments. Conventional approaches address CSI feedback and prediction as separate, cascaded tasks, which is inherently suboptimal. This paper proposes a novel end-to-end learning framework that unifies the entire process from CSI estimation and feedback to latent-space prediction and downlink precoding. At the core of our framework is a new, computationally efficient channel prediction model, the Patched Multi-Layer SAMformer (PMSAM), which operates directly on the compressed latent representation of the channel. To enhance robustness and generalization, PMSAM is trained using Sharpness-Aware Minimization (SAM). Furthermore, our framework uniquely incorporates uplink Sounding Reference Signals (SRS) by exploiting weak channel reciprocity, using uplink information to refine downlink prediction accuracy. Extensive simulation results show that the proposed framework achieves lower prediction error and higher downlink spectral efficiency than representative cascaded feedback-and-prediction baselines under the considered feedback budget.
